.TH TRASHSYNC 1 "2026-10-08" "trashsync" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
trashsync \- sync KDE's trashrc Empty flag with the real trash state
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B trashsync
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B trashsync
recomputes whether the trash is empty and stores the result in the
.B [Status]
.B Empty
key of
.IR ~/.config/trashrc ,
which KDE applications such as
.BR dolphin (1)
read to decide whether to enable their
.I Empty Trash
action.
.P
It is a workaround for KDE bug 293651: when a non\-KDE application
(for example
.BR losslesscut ,
which trashes files through GIO/Electron) moves them into a volume
trash, KDE never updates the flag, so
.B dolphin
leaves
.I Empty Trash
greyed out even though the trash is not empty. This helper rewrites the
flag so the action becomes available again.
.P
The trash is treated as non\-empty if either
.I ~/.local/share/Trash/info
or
.I /mnt/shared/.Trash\-1000/info
contains at least one
.I .trashinfo
file. The flag is written only when its value actually changes, so the
helper is cheap to run repeatedly.
.P
It takes no options, and requires
.BR kreadconfig6 (1)
and
.BR kwriteconfig6 (1).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, whether or not the flag needed changing.
.TP
.B 1
A required command was missing or a configuration call failed.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/trashrc
KDE trash state file; its
.B [Status] Empty
key is read and rewritten.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/Trash/info
Home trash metadata directory (checked).
.TP
.I /mnt/shared/.Trash\-1000/info
Shared NTFS volume trash metadata directory (checked).
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/shared\-trash\-sync.path
User path unit that runs
.B trashsync
whenever a watched trash changes.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/shared\-trash\-sync.timer
User timer that runs
.B trashsync
every 30 seconds as a safety net. A path unit's inotify watch stops
working if the filesystem it watches is unmounted and remounted, so the
timer guarantees the flag is corrected even then.
.TP
.I ~/.config/systemd/user/shared\-trash\-sync.service
Oneshot service activated by both units above.
.SH EXAMPLES
Sync the flag by hand after trashing files from a non\-KDE app:
.IP
.EX
trashsync
.EE
.P
Re\-arm the change watcher after mounting
.IR /mnt/shared :
.IP
.EX
systemctl \-\-user restart shared\-trash\-sync.path
.EE
.P
Inspect the path unit and the timer:
.IP
.EX
systemctl \-\-user list\-units 'shared\-trash\-sync*' \-\-all
systemctl \-\-user list\-timers 'shared\-trash\-sync*'
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dolphin (1),
.BR kreadconfig6 (1),
.BR kwriteconfig6 (1),
.BR systemd.path (5),
.BR systemd.timer (5)
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
